3
00:00:03.790 --> 00:00:06.800
Cynthia Germanotta does it all.

4
00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:08.430
She is a business woman,

5
00:00:08.430 --> 00:00:13.230
a Goodwill Ambassador and mother to Natalie and Stephanie,

6
00:00:13.230 --> 00:00:17.260
better known to the world by her stage name, Lady Gaga.

7
00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:20.880
Cynthia knew that Stephanie was unique from a young age,

8
00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:22.450
but says Stephanie's uniqueness

9
00:00:22.450 --> 00:00:25.090
and fierce independence made her the target

10
00:00:25.090 --> 00:00:26.880
of some high school bullies.

11
00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:30.940
Cynthia struggled with how to best support her daughter

12
00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:33.900
and despite decades of global success,

13
00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:37.030
neither mother nor daughter has ever forgotten

14
00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:42.030
how it felt to be ostracized for just being yourself.

15
00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:47.880
And so in 2012, they founded the Born This Way Foundation

16
00:00:48.620 --> 00:00:51.430
to support the mental health of young people.

17
00:00:51.430 --> 00:00:54.240
They've taken direct steps to help children

18
00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:58.430
and their parents access resources, take direct action

19
00:00:58.430 --> 00:01:00.270
and build community.

20
00:01:00.270 --> 00:01:02.350
They're on the right track, baby.

21
00:01:02.350 --> 00:01:04.430
And we're so thankful to them

22
00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:09.163
for creating a kinder, braver world for all of us.

23
00:01:12.501 --> 00:01:16.606
Ladies and gentlemen, please welcome Cynthia Germanotta.

24
00:01:16.606 --> 00:01:21.606
(audience clap)
(upbeat music)

25
00:01:30.295 --> 00:01:31.336
I'm gonna cry.

26
00:01:31.336 --> 00:01:34.391
I love you, you're wonderful.

27
00:01:34.391 --> 00:01:37.391
Thank you so much for coming here.

28
00:01:38.834 --> 00:01:40.694
Thank you.
Thank you for having me.

29
00:01:40.694 --> 00:01:42.698
I'm so grateful that you would come here.

30
00:01:42.698 --> 00:01:44.630
I'm so grateful that you would have me.

31
00:01:44.630 --> 00:01:46.257
I'm pinching myself.

32
00:01:46.257 --> 00:01:49.322
My goodness, you're so beautiful too by the the way.

33
00:01:49.322 --> 00:01:50.155
You're so beautiful.

34
00:01:50.155 --> 00:01:53.610
And you're so beautiful.
(audience clap)

35
00:01:53.610 --> 00:01:58.110
I'm just so honored that you had come here today.

36
00:01:58.110 --> 00:02:01.770
What was the spark may I ask

37
00:02:01.770 --> 00:02:04.190
for starting the Born This Way Foundation?

38
00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:06.840
Was there a moment or an instance?

39
00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:09.000
I know there's history there.

40
00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:10.980
The things that inspired the foundation,

41
00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:12.790
they were a couple of things.

42
00:02:12.790 --> 00:02:14.540 line:15%
The first was kindness

43
00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:17.800 line:15%
or what I would call the absence of kindness.

44
00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:21.390 line:15%
She's written about something she calls negative space,

45
00:02:21.390 --> 00:02:26.390
and it's a moment when somebody is unkind to you

46
00:02:26.710 --> 00:02:28.540
and there's a negative space.

47
00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:30.930
And you as a human being have an opportunity

48
00:02:30.930 --> 00:02:33.980
to fill that space with kindness.

49
00:02:33.980 --> 00:02:35.740
And because there were many moments

50
00:02:35.740 --> 00:02:39.020
where that space wasn't filled for her,

51
00:02:39.020 --> 00:02:41.010
it affected her very, very deeply.

52
00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:44.440
And kindness had a really transformative impact

53
00:02:44.440 --> 00:02:45.370
on her life.

54
00:02:45.370 --> 00:02:50.230
And because it was absent, she developed anxiety

55
00:02:50.230 --> 00:02:53.510
and depression at a very, very young age.

56
00:02:53.510 --> 00:02:56.480
The other inspiration were the incredible stories

57
00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:59.460
that we heard from young people all over the world

58
00:02:59.460 --> 00:03:01.640
as she started to tour and travel,

59
00:03:01.640 --> 00:03:04.510
and we made it a point to sit down with them

60
00:03:04.510 --> 00:03:07.800
and talk to them and understand how they were feeling

61
00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:10.090
and what was happening in their lives.

62
00:03:10.090 --> 00:03:13.505
And the stories were so similar to hers.

63
00:03:13.505 --> 00:03:17.210
And that said, these young people,

64
00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:19.050
they wanted to be part of a change.

65
00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:21.867
And they were like, "Gaga, how did you do it?

66
00:03:21.867 --> 00:03:24.227
"How did you turn your life around?

67
00:03:24.227 --> 00:03:26.070
"What were the things that you did?"

68
00:03:26.070 --> 00:03:30.940
And those stories impacted both of us very deeply.

69
00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:33.130
And I remember one instance,

70
00:03:33.130 --> 00:03:35.320
we were in Paris and she was touring

71
00:03:35.320 --> 00:03:38.750 line:15%
and we heard just incredible heartfelt stories.

72
00:03:38.750 --> 00:03:41.630 line:15%
And we got on the plane to come home

73
00:03:41.630 --> 00:03:44.190 line:15%
and we fasten your seatbelt.

74
00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:45.023
We strapped in

75
00:03:45.023 --> 00:03:48.160
and she looked at me and said, "Mom, it's time."

76
00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:50.080
And I said, "Time for what?"

77
00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:53.530
And she said, "It's time to help these kids."

78
00:03:53.530 --> 00:03:57.050
Now, she's a kid at the same time telling me

79
00:03:57.050 --> 00:04:01.310
that she wants to help other young people be kinder

80
00:04:01.310 --> 00:04:05.030
and braver to one another and have resources,

81
00:04:05.030 --> 00:04:07.230
be better equipped to deal with their struggles

82
00:04:07.230 --> 00:04:08.770
than she felt that she was.

83
00:04:08.770 --> 00:04:11.426
And that was the real genesis of the foundation.

84
00:04:11.426 --> 00:04:14.009 line:15%
(upbeat music)

